From: Betterr <51264180+Star-caorui@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 17:53:13 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] LineageSettingsProvider: Notify key URI on delete

Deleting a setting through call(), as "settings delete --lineage" does,
notified observers with the table's URI, while putting one notifies them
with the setting's own URI. Observers registered on a setting with
notifyForDescendants then get a URI they do not know. The input settings
observer in system_server looks the URI up in its map and calls the
result, so

  settings delete --lineage system swap_volume_keys_on_rotation

crashes system_server with a NullPointerException.

Pass the setting's URI to deleteForUser(), which resolves the table from
it as well, so the deletion is announced like the insertion.

Change-Id: Ib753763846a948cb3ca68023d8c0185821d428c7
---
 .../lineageos/lineagesettings/LineageSettingsProvider.java    | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/src/org/lineageos/lineagesettings/LineageSettingsProvider.java b/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/src/org/lineageos/lineagesettings/LineageSettingsProvider.java
index 79b898dc..5b5dab6f 100644
--- a/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/src/org/lineageos/lineagesettings/LineageSettingsProvider.java
+++ b/packages/LineageSettingsProvider/src/org/lineageos/lineagesettings/LineageSettingsProvider.java
@@ -220,8 +220,8 @@ public class LineageSettingsProvider extends ContentProvider {
 
     // Helper for call() CALL_METHOD_DELETE_* methods
     private Bundle callHelperDelete(int callingUserId, Uri contentUri, String key) {
-        final int rowsDeleted = deleteForUser(callingUserId, contentUri, NAME_SELECTION,
-                new String[]{ key });
+        final int rowsDeleted = deleteForUser(callingUserId, Uri.withAppendedPath(contentUri, key),
+                NAME_SELECTION, new String[]{ key });
         final Bundle ret = new Bundle();
         ret.putInt(RESULT_ROWS_DELETED, rowsDeleted);
         return ret;
